 </section>

 <!-- 03 WEBSITE -->
 <section class="sec">
  <div class="sl m"><span><span class="n">03</span> · The website</span><span>Hand-built, no frameworks</span></div>
  <div class="sh"><h2 class="rv">A website that tells the story by itself.</h2><p class="rv d1">Agency sites usually just list services. I wanted visitors to <b>watch a shop get fixed</b>, then play with the product, all in one dependency-free HTML file.</p></div>
  <div class="gal">
   <div class="shot rv"><div class="vf"><span class="c tl"></span><span class="c tr"></span><div class="hd"><span>FIG. 01 · SCROLL STORY</span><span></span></div><img src="/img/story.jpg" alt="Scroll story section"></div><h4>A storefront that fixes itself</h4><p>A pinned, hand-drawn SVG shop whose problems (“No website”, “12 reviews”) get <b>fixed one by one as you scroll</b>, synced to a step list and progress bar.</p></div>
   <div class="shot rv d1"><div class="vf"><span class="c tl"></span><span class="c tr"></span><div class="hd"><span>FIG. 02 · PHYSICS</span><span></span></div><img src="/img/phys.jpg" alt="Physics section"></div><h4>Review stands you can throw</h4><p>A <b>custom 2D physics engine</b>: gravity, bounce, circle collisions, drag-and-fling with real velocity, and a sleep state when everything rests.</p></div>
   <div class="shot rv"><div class="vf"><span class="c tl"></span><span class="c tr"></span><div class="hd"><span>FIG. 03 · SERVICES</span><span></span></div><img src="/img/svc.jpg" alt="Services section"></div><h4>A blueprint design system</h4><p>A 48px grid, crosshair marks, figure labels and a three-font type system, all driven by <b>CSS custom properties</b>.</p></div>
   <div class="shot rv d1"><div class="vf"><span class="c tl"></span><span class="c tr"></span><div class="hd"><span>FIG. 04 · PRICING</span><span></span></div><img src="/img/price.jpg" alt="Pricing section"></div><h4>Accessible by default</h4><p>Pricing tabs with <b>arrow-key support</b>, a live San José clock, copy-to-clipboard contact buttons and hover previews on the work list.</p></div>
  </div>
 </section>

 <!-- 04 THROW -->
 <section class="sec" id="throw">
  <div class="sl m"><span><span class="n">04</span> · Try it</span><span>The physics, live</span></div>
  <div class="sh"><h2 class="rv">Go ahead. Throw a review stand.</h2><p class="rv d1">This is a small rebuild of the physics from the site. <b>Grab anything and fling it.</b> It runs on the same ideas: gravity, collisions, velocity from your drag, and sleeping when still.</p></div>
  <div class="phys rv">
   <div class="cv" id="cv"><canvas id="pc"></canvas><span class="tag">FIG. 05 · DRAG + FLING</span><span class="hint">GRAB ONE ↓</span></div>
   <div class="r"><div class="m" style="display:block;border:0;padding:0 0 10px">How it works</div>
    <div><span>01</span><p><b>Gravity &amp; bounce</b> with energy loss on every hit</p></div>
    <div><span>02</span><p><b>Circle collisions</b> push objects apart and trade momentum</p></div>
    <div><span>03</span><p><b>Fling velocity</b> comes from your last pointer movements</p></div>
    <div><span>04</span><p><b>Sleep state:</b> the loop stops when nothing moves, saving the CPU</p></div>
    <button class="drop" id="drop">Drop them again</button></div>
  </div>
  <div class="perf rv"><div><b>60<em>fps</em></b><small>while scrolling: rAF-batched work, transform-only animation</small></div><div><b>~60<em>KB</em></b><small>one HTML file plus fonts, no build step</small></div><div><b>AA</b><small>color contrast chosen to meet WCAG AA</small></div><div><b>0</b><small>animations for people who turn on reduced motion</small></div></div>
  <div class="note rv"><div class="m">The hard part</div><p>The first version <b>lagged</b>. I fixed it by removing blur effects, moving all animation to transforms, batching scroll work into requestAnimationFrame, only touching the DOM when state actually changes, and putting the physics loop to sleep when idle. It now holds 60 fps.</p></div>
 </section>

